**Key idea:** In `uvm_reg_adapter`, `reg2bus` translates abstract register operations into physical bus sequence items, while `bus2reg` unpacks completed bus transactions back into register values and status flags.

```mermaid
sequenceDiagram
  participant TEST as Sequence / Test
  participant RAL as uvm_reg
  participant ADAPT as uvm_reg_adapter
  participant SQR as Bus Sequencer & Driver
  TEST->>RAL: reg.write(status, 32'hDEADBEEF)
  RAL->>ADAPT: Calls reg2bus(uvm_reg_bus_op rw)
  ADAPT-->>RAL: Returns protocol item (e.g. apb_seq_item)
  RAL->>SQR: Dispatches bus item to sequencer
  SQR->>SQR: Driver executes pin transfer
  SQR-->>RAL: Bus transfer completes
  RAL->>ADAPT: Calls bus2reg(bus_item, uvm_reg_bus_op rw)
  ADAPT-->>RAL: Updates rw.data and rw.status (UVM_IS_OK)
  RAL-->>TEST: Returns status to caller
```

### Code
```systemverilog
class reg2apb_adapter extends uvm_reg_adapter;
  `uvm_object_utils(reg2apb_adapter)

  function new(string name = "reg2apb_adapter");
    super.new(name);
    supports_byte_enable = 1;
    provides_responses   = 0;
  endfunction

  virtual function uvm_sequence_item reg2bus(const ref uvm_reg_bus_op rw);
    apb_seq_item apb = apb_seq_item::type_id::create("apb");
    apb.write = (rw.kind == UVM_WRITE);
    apb.addr  = rw.addr;
    apb.data  = rw.data;
    apb.strb  = rw.byte_en;
    return apb;
  endfunction

  virtual function void bus2reg(uvm_sequence_item bus_item, ref uvm_reg_bus_op rw);
    apb_seq_item apb;
    if (!$cast(apb, bus_item))
      `uvm_fatal("CONVERT", "Provided bus_item is not of type apb_seq_item")
    rw.kind   = apb.write ? UVM_WRITE : UVM_READ;
    rw.addr   = apb.addr;
    rw.data   = apb.data;
    rw.status = (apb.slverr) ? UVM_NOT_OK : UVM_IS_OK;
  endfunction
endclass
```

### Corner cases & pitfalls
- **Byte Enable Handling:** If the bus supports byte strobes, set `supports_byte_enable = 1` in the adapter constructor and map `rw.byte_en` in `reg2bus`.
- **Response Handling:** If the bus driver returns separate response items asynchronously, set `provides_responses = 1` in the adapter.

### Follow-ups
- Can `reg2bus` return null? No, returning null halts register sequence execution with a fatal error.
- Why are `reg2bus` and `bus2reg` functions and not tasks? They are pure computational format converters and must not consume simulation time.

